\ Back-edge invariance, negative case: a counted-loop combinator whose body is
\ not stack-neutral across the bounded row. Each iteration leaves an extra value
\ (`0`) above the row, so the recursive back-edge shape does not match the loop
\ entry. The AOT compiler must reject this cleanly under
\ --interpreter-fallback=false rather than miscompile a drifting stack.
bad-loop: ( n quot -- ) [
  over 0 >
  [ dup 2dip 0 swap -- swap bad-loop ]
  [ 2drop ]
  if
] ;
3 [ "tick" print-line ] bad-loop
